      "value": "@{610e7ee617aec43b2a62c4a6|full_name} This is exatly what i don't want! if somebody should decide what is the right amount of players to show, than this is VRChat with input from settings (maybe something like a \"target fps\" slider). NOT the world creator! Ex. You can make jet windows not transparent anymore above 40m. Than it makes sense for me to hide player beyond 40m to set by the world creator.\n\nBut DON'T adjust my maximum distance based on any caluculation with my FPS! Everybody has different comfort with the amount of frames they see. and i also don't want to setup my FPS target in every world. \n\nTLDR; You can hide avatars which i don't need to render. But do NOT hide anything based on my FPS!",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
